A||N||17||David Johnson||87 GT dash speaker replacement||||1||
Z||000000||David Johnson||12-08-1999||12:03 PM||||Can they be accessed from above the dash ?<BR>How bad a job is it. Where can I get best price/ quality on speakers ? Thanks, David J||||reg||1
Z||000001||Wolfhound||12-08-1999||12:37 PM||||Yes, They come out from the top. The covers have 4 plastic pins. One at each corner.<BR> Pry up gently in the middle of each (side), using a butter knife or anything dull enough not to damage the fabric cover. lift only until the speaker covers bottom is flush with the top of the dash. at this point  it will lift on out. If you try to completely remove one side at a time you stand the chance of breaking the plastic pins on the opposite side. Once out four 7mm screws nuts hold the speaker in.<BR> I adapted the the conection on the old speaker to the new so I wouldn,t have to cut the original connection off the speaker wires, since they were different.<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||12-08-1999||02:38 PM||||It's easy to replace the front speakers, do just as Wolfie said. The factory size is 4" X 10" which is readily available, but unfortunately your choices are sort of limited. Speaker selection is greatly a matter of preference, but I put Pioneer coaxial speakers (TS-A4103) in my Batmobile last summer at a cost of about $75 (U.S.) and I think they sound pretty good. Just don't get the cheap bargain no-brand speakers. The connectors will be different, so you need to splice in the new connectors or buy adapters if you don't want to cut the factory wires.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 12-08-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dave85||12-08-1999||04:04 PM||||Autotoys.com has Pioneer 4x10 3 ways for under $80. Someone on the fourm has 6x9's in there dash. <BR>Dave||||reg||1
Z||000004||ka4nkf||12-08-1999||07:33 PM||||I bought some from radio shack and they sound just as good as the orignal speakers.<BR>around $14.00 each. I also took the connection off the old speakers and put them on the new speakers to keep from cutting the wires.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gokart||12-08-1999||08:58 PM||||I got the 6x9's in my dash! If you want to do this, which to me is well worth while for quality sound you can only get from 6x9's, is get the factory one's out, take a small hand hack saw and cut the openings to meet the outer edges, leaving one peg hole that the grills fit in the top right and bottom left, use small cable ties through the speaker holes then through the peg holes and tighten them flush. Then the grills go right on and you can't tell the difference except SOUND! The only prob and I can't remember now that one speaker I had to feed from the bottom and up and one I slipped in from the top! Good luck!||||reg||3
Z||000006||batboy||12-08-1999||10:06 PM||||No offense Ka4nkf, but the sound quality of the original speakers sucks big time and will not hold up to the newer high power stereo systems. The whole point of replacing the factory speakers with better ones is for it to sound much better and to handle higher watts.||||reg||1
Z||000007||David Johnson||12-09-1999||12:04 AM||||this list is great !  Where have you been all my life !  <BR>Thanks for all the help, I really appreciate it.<BR>David Johnson (killer 87 GT)||||reg||1
Z||000008||Wolfhound||12-09-1999||07:18 AM||||Gokart, Did you mount the 6x9s against the backside of the dash rather than sitting on top?||||reg||5
Z||000009||Gokart||12-09-1999||09:07 PM||||Yes, at least on one side, I think the passengers because I had to feed it through the bottom cause it was too tight a fit to get it in from the top. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||2FAST4U||12-10-1999||12:27 AM||||Chruchfield list several high quality 4X10 speakers.||||reg||1
Z||000011||batboy||12-10-1999||06:47 AM||||I guess when you say Crutchfield has several speakers, that means two. My catalog only shows two models of Pioneer 4" X 10" speakers (TS-A4103 and TS-A4105).||||reg||1
Z||000012||Monkeyman||12-10-1999||01:28 PM||||The online store lists the same.  Just 2.  That's a shame since they're supposed to be the biggest and best!||||reg||1
Z||000013||ChadMan||12-10-1999||02:06 PM||||It's hard to find good 4x10 speakers.  I put a pair of Pyle Driver 2-ways in my 84, then transferred them to my 88.  They cost me $90 and they sound as good today as they did the day I bought 'em.  I don't think Pyle makes full-range car speakers anymore, just subs.<P>I've heard the Pioneer 3-ways, and they're pretty good.  I think Kenwood makes some too.||||reg||9
Z||000014||Standard||12-10-1999||07:27 PM||||I installed the Pioneer 4x10 2 ways in mine and I think they sound great!  I have the stock system with my discman hooked up to it, and I can feel the bass just fine when it's cranked up, and not too much distortion, either.||||reg||14
Z||000015||william_thorniii||12-10-1999||07:44 PM||||GoKart,<P>You have the right idea but why if you are interested in SQ did you go with a 6X9 in the place of a 6" round?  I thought many times about placing the 6.25" (Polk db) mids in my dash openings.  Unfortunately with the stock locations, I could not get the quality I wanted which is why I went with custom kick pods that rest on the dead pedals.  <P>Everyone,<P>I hate to be a prick and I have been biting my tongue for quite a while.... but anything less than a 8" woofer is incapable of producing "base".  It is simple physics.  Now things can be done to make a midrange speaker move slower to create lower sounds, but they are not truly in the bass range.  The same applies for the Performance Sound option on our cars.  Although they significantly icrease the sound quality that which both the 4x10's and 4x6 plates lacked and they also increase the amount of mid-to-low range sounds they are not a subwoofer.  You don't have to conform to these standard simply make a note of them.  If you were to state that your Fiero had a subwoofer up underneath the dash, most stereophiles would be impressed.  Unfortunately, upon further inspection they would probably laugh at you for your previous statements.  Just something to think about.<P>Later,<P>William T. Thorn, III ||||reg||1
Z||000016||jhogans||12-10-1999||08:16 PM||||william_thorniii,<P>do you have any pictures of your kickpods or any of your installations.  I would like to see what you did to get some ideas for my car audio install.||||reg||5
Z||000017||Gokart||12-10-1999||08:33 PM||||6X9's fit up front, but I can't imagine how anyone would get 6" round speakers there! I got PLENTY of bass from my home entertainment subwoofer on the passenger side floor. Replaced the home speaker with a 12" dual voice coil auto speaker and 280 watts powering it up! IT CRANKS!||||reg||6
